<title>THAILAND: Thailand might delay corn import schedule.</title>
<headline>Thailand might delay corn import schedule.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand might delay the import schedule for tariff-free corn from February 20-June 30 set earlier, a senior Commerce Ministry source said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The move is to encourage the animal feed industry to use more local corn following a rise in fresh supplies, and thus support the domestic price, the source told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Farmers complained that the industry slowed down buying, awaiting imports and consequently pushing the prices down,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;But what the new schedule would be depended on the cabinet decision,&quot; he said, adding that the proposal was likely to be presented to the cabinet for approval on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The price of corn was quoted around 4.20-4.30 baht ($0.17) a kg this week, according to trade sources.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
